Cards a saved game state could not hold (Commander Duels v0.9.9, recovery). Every format.

Reason: a checkpoint (docs/engine/recovery.md) is the game written down by Java's serialization.
XMage never serializes a game, it copies its objects, so nothing had ever noticed that a few classes
its cards use cannot be written: a game with one of those cards in it could not be checkpointed, and
so could not be taken up after an interruption. Writing every card of the card database once
(SerializableCardsTest, 33,612 cards) found 37 that could not be, for six reasons, all of them a
class or a functional interface that is not Serializable:

- BeholdType (20 cards, Lorwyn Eclipsed's "behold a ..."): now Serializable; one read back is the
  one instance of its subtype (readResolve), as getBeholdType keeps them.
- FaceVillainousChoice and VillainousChoice (4 cards found, 7 in all): now Serializable.
- CreateTokenCopyTargetEffect.PermanentModifier (3 cards found; 13 use it, most of them only in
  an effect made as an ability resolves): now extends Serializable, so the lambdas given to
  setPermanentModifier are.
- ModifyObjectAllMultiZoneEffect.ObjectModifier (7 cards: Arcane Adaptation, Maskwood Nexus,
  Conspiracy, Leyline of Transformation and the like): now extends Serializable.
- CreateXXTokenExiledEffectManaValueEffect's token maker (Skyclave Apparition, Severance Priest):
  its Function becomes TokenMaker, a Function that is Serializable.
- GainAbilityWithAttachmentEffect's Consumer (The Dominion Bracelet): becomes AbilityModifier, a
  Consumer that is Serializable.

Nothing changes in how any card plays: the types say only that their objects may be written. After
the patch the same test writes every card.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage's game objects are serializable, or Commander Duels' checkpoints no longer use
Java's serialization.

